<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> Co-Prosperity Sphere was a concept proclaimed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> for a bloc of Asian nations under Japanese leadership, free of Western colonial rule. In practice it served to justify Japanese expansion and the economic exploitation of occupied territories during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. It features in accounts of the Japanese imperial economy and its wartime resource needs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greater-east-asia-co-prosperity-sphere.jpg" alt="Greater East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_1943_propaganda_booklet_1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
